CON-23: update rain gages that only control rules read

A gage is advanced through its record only if it is flagged as used, and
only subcatchments and unit hydrographs set the flag. A gage read only by a
rule premise or VARIABLE ("GAGE G2 INTENSITY", "GAGE G2 6") was never
updated, and getRainValue() returned 0 for it, so the rule never acted.
Three changes:
- getPremiseVariable() flags a gage named in a rule as used;
- gage_readParams() no longer clears the flag (Gage[] is calloc'd), so a
  [CONTROLS] or [HYDROGRAPHS] section placed before [RAINGAGES] keeps its
  mark (this also restores RDII inflow, which was 0 in that order);
- in a model without subcatchments, where runoff_execute() never runs,
  routing_execute() updates the gages and their past-rain totals itself.

Requires: NUM-19

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-23_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
index e423886..30d14e8 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
@@ -1211,6 +1211,7 @@ int getPremiseVariable(char *tok[], int nToks, int *k, struct TVariable *v)
         if (index < 0)
             return error_setInpError(ERR_NAME, tok[n]);
         object = r_GAGE;
+        Gage[index].isUsed = TRUE;   // so that the gage gets updated
         break;
 
     case r_NODE:
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/gage.c b/src/legacy/engine/gage.c
index 69f7ce0..929f8fb 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/gage.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/gage.c
@@ -125,7 +125,6 @@ int gage_readParams(int gageIndex, char* tok[], int ntoks)
     }
     Gage[gageIndex].unitsFactor = 1.0;
     Gage[gageIndex].coGage = -1;
-    Gage[gageIndex].isUsed = FALSE;
     return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
index 94892d5..feead0c 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ static int* SortedLinks;
 static int  NextEvent;
